# Commands the docs name on purpose because they do NOT exist. Each line is a
# deliberate mention; deleting the line would make the checker demand the
# sentence be removed, and the sentence is the useful part.

# docs/boot-v2.md: "There is deliberately no `apex boot ack` verb: the notice is
# cleared automatically on a boot where no entry is exhausted, so it tracks
# reality instead of tracking whether somebody dismissed it."
apex boot ack

# docs/recovery.md: "Adding an `apex recover previous` verb would have been a
# second name for an operation that already exists" (namely `sudo apex rollback`).
apex recover previous

# docs/rollback.md: "An earlier version of this document claimed
# `apex reset --keep-home` shipped in M3. It never did; the verb above is what
# exists." Naming the retired claim is how a reader who saw the old doc knows.
apex reset

# docs/fleet.md is a DESIGN, and it says so in its first two sentences: "No code
# here exists. There is no `apex fleet` verb, no enrolment record, no server."
# The verb names are the shape being proposed, and a checker that demanded they
# be removed would turn a design document into a document that cannot describe
# what it is designing. They leave this file on the day the verb ships.
apex fleet
apex fleet join
apex fleet leave
apex fleet status

